# GrowFlow — Phase 05
# Application & Integration Architecture

**Status:** 🔒 FROZEN / AUTHORITATIVE  
**Phase:** 05  
**Scope:** V1 application, backend, data, AI, integration, reliability, security, and operational architecture  
**Depends on:** Phase 01, Phase 02, Phase 03, Phase 04

---

## Purpose

Phase 05 is the technical architecture contract beneath the frontend specification.

It defines **where canonical state lives, how requests flow, how domain rules execute, how AI is orchestrated, how long-running work survives browser disconnects, how events reach the frontend, how RAG remains derived, how external integrations are isolated, and how security/observability/reliability are enforced.**

### Frozen system direction

```text
Frontend
   ↓ REST / SSE
FastAPI
   ↓
Application Services
   ↓
Domain Services
   ↓
PostgreSQL / Canonical State
   ↓
Events + Jobs + AI + RAG + Integrations
   ↓
Validated Persistence
   ↓
Notifications / SSE / Derived Views
   ↓
Frontend Reconciliation
```

### Core invariant

> **Everything important eventually resolves to canonical, authorized, validated state.**

AI may generate. RAG may retrieve. Workers may process. Events may distribute. SSE may deliver. Documents may represent. Analytics may analyze. The frontend may present. None of these silently replaces canonical domain ownership.

---

## Phase 05 Governance

- No architectural decision from Phases 01–04 is silently changed.
- Implementation-specific values are explicitly labeled rather than guessed.
- Every high-risk workflow has an owner, state model, failure model, security boundary, and observability path.
- Every derived representation has a defined source.
- Every asynchronous workflow is independent of browser connectivity.
- Every sensitive operation has explicit authorization.
- Every future architecture change is recorded through a Technical Decision Record.

