# 1. Phase 05 Objective

**Purpose:** Define the complete technical architecture behind GrowFlow so every frontend operation, backend use case, AI workflow, integration, event, and persistence boundary has an explicit home.

## Required Decisions / Rules

- Define the complete system boundary and runtime components.
- Identify ownership, dependencies, data flow, failure boundaries, and integration boundaries.
- Trace important operations from user action to canonical persistence and back to the frontend.
- Never hide an unresolved architecture choice behind an assumption.

## Inputs / Outputs / Boundaries

- **Input:** Define the complete technical architecture behind GrowFlow so every frontend operation, backend use case, AI workflow, integration, event, and persistence boundary has an explicit home.
- **Canonical owner:** GrowFlow backend/domain/database unless another owner is explicitly named.
- **Frontend role:** Render authorized state, submit commands, consume results, and reconcile after asynchronous events.
- **Security:** Authorization and scope must be enforced before sensitive access or processing.
- **Reliability:** Failure must be observable, recoverable where appropriate, and prevented from creating hidden canonical divergence.
- **Testing:** The behavior must be represented in the appropriate unit, integration, contract, or E2E layer.

