# Non-Negotiable System Invariants

1. Browser never directly mutates PostgreSQL.
2. Browser never directly calls an AI provider.
3. Browser never directly accesses RAG infrastructure.
4. AI agents never bypass validation.
5. AI output never silently becomes canonical state.
6. RAG never becomes the canonical project database.
7. Activity never becomes the canonical event store.
8. SSE never becomes the source of truth.
9. Frontend authorization never replaces backend authorization.
10. Definition updates never silently mutate existing instances.
11. Background jobs never depend on an open browser connection.
12. Provider secrets never reach frontend clients.
13. GitHub secrets never reach ordinary API responses.
14. Admin investigation never becomes unrestricted impersonation.
15. Expensive duplicate AI requests are controlled.
16. Canonical mutations and required events cannot silently diverge.
17. Derived projections are rebuildable where claimed.
18. Important asynchronous workflows have terminal success/failure states.
19. High-risk operations are observable and traceable.
20. Architecture changes are explicit and recorded.

